1
00:00:03,109 --> 00:00:06,037
Mila catches a snowflake on her mitten:

2
00:00:06,087 --> 00:00:08,405
a tiny star, with six branches.

3
00:00:08,455 --> 00:00:09,322
Another one…

4
00:00:09,372 --> 00:00:10,620
six branches too!

5
00:00:10,670 --> 00:00:12,453
Never five, never seven.

6
00:00:12,503 --> 00:00:13,114
Why six?

7
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:16,877
Under the magnifying glass, every snowflake is different,

8
00:00:16,927 --> 00:00:18,258
but all have six branches.

9
00:00:18,308 --> 00:00:20,276
Noah draws one with too many branches:

10
00:00:20,326 --> 00:00:21,600
impossible in real life!

11
00:00:22,372 --> 00:00:23,886
Discovery mission!

12
00:00:26,402 --> 00:00:27,060
Mini mode!

13
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:28,193
In an icy cloud,

14
00:00:28,243 --> 00:00:31,663
a very cold droplet freezes onto a speck of dust.

15
00:00:31,713 --> 00:00:33,859
Then water vapor turns straight

16
00:00:33,909 --> 00:00:35,537
into ice all around it.

17
00:00:36,328 --> 00:00:39,913
When freezing, water molecules always line up the same way:

18
00:00:39,963 --> 00:00:41,638
in hexagons, with six sides.

19
00:00:41,688 --> 00:00:43,856
So the crystal grows with six sides,

20
00:00:43,906 --> 00:00:45,015
then six branches.

21
00:00:45,792 --> 00:00:50,269
As it falls, the snowflake travels through air that is more or less cold and humid:

22
00:00:50,319 --> 00:00:51,906
its branches grow differently.

23
00:00:51,956 --> 00:00:53,651
But all six live the same story:

24
00:00:53,701 --> 00:00:54,574
they stay alike.

25
00:00:55,341 --> 00:00:58,571
And since no two snowflakes make exactly the same journey,

26
00:00:58,621 --> 00:00:59,533
no two are alike.

27
00:00:59,583 --> 00:01:02,184
Billions of six-branched stars, all different!

28
00:01:02,968 --> 00:01:05,283
That's why snowflakes have six branches.

29
00:01:06,509 --> 00:01:08,253
Ice builds itself in hexagons;

30
00:01:08,303 --> 00:01:10,876
so every snowflake grows with six branches.

31
00:01:11,719 --> 00:01:13,402
With an adult, on a snowy day:

32
00:01:13,452 --> 00:01:17,679
catch snowflakes on a dark glove and look at them with a magnifying glass.

33
00:01:17,729 --> 00:01:18,827
Count the branches!

34
00:01:19,631 --> 00:01:21,573
And why do the seasons change?

35
00:01:21,623 --> 00:01:22,951
The answer tomorrow.
